# E2E vs UI changes

When changing operator-facing UI (copy, layout, nav, Settings, wizard, modals,
workspace tabs, `data-*`), check `scripts/e2e-*.cjs` in the **same PR**.

PR CI only runs CRUD, install-health, and host-port-probe (`e2e:smoke` is local). Settings,
Mods, clone/import/move, RCON, and log-retention suites will rot unless you
update and run the scripts they actually click.

1. Search `scripts/e2e` for the old label, role, or `data-*`.
2. Prefer helpers in `scripts/e2e-launch.cjs` (`openSettingsCategory`,
   `pickPathField`, `waitForOverview`, `YARK_E2E_USER_DATA`).
3. `npm run build` then the **affected** `npm run e2e:*` on Windows. Skip
   `e2e:crash-reattach` / `e2e:clone-copy-real` unless that path changed.

